#1 Inline syntax

| Syntax | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `*[strong]` | Strong emphasis |
| `/[emphasis]` | Emphasis |
| `/*[strong emphasis]` | Strong plus emphasis |
| `-[underline]` | Underline |
| `~[deleted]` | Strikethrough |
| `=[highlight]` | Highlight |
| `^[2]` | Superscript |
| `_[i]` | Subscript |
| `` `code` `` | Inline code |
| `[[target|label]]` | Wiki link |
| `[label](https://example.com)` | External link |
| `[&smith2024]` | Citation |
| `[^note]` | Footnote |

Inline syntax can be nested and escaped characters remain literal. Every node keeps a source range so tools and diagnostics can point back to the original text.
